# Target: xmarre/ComfyUI-Spectrum-MiniMax-H3 @ v0.2.20 (commit ce9d35e)
#
# Cause: ComfyUI commit 2504e68d (PDD LoRA support, MiniMax H3) changed
#       comfy.ldm.minimax.model.FinalLayer.forward to 7 parameters:
#       (self, x, t_emb, video_seg, audio_seg, sigma, sample_sigmas, shifts).
#       Spectrum's residual output-head forecast still calls the old 4-arg form
#       at comfyui_spectrum_h3/minimax_h3.py:452. On ComfyUI >= 0.34 the call
#       raises TypeError, which the guard except (RuntimeError, TypeError,
#       ValueError) at minimax_h3.py:~431 swallows via
#       runtime.disable_experiment('residual output-head evaluation failed: ...').
#       Result: the forecast speedup is silently disabled on every sampling step
#       - no error surfaces, the model just runs the slower full path.
#
# Fix: detect at call time whether the live final_layer.forward accepts the PDD
#       arguments (presence of the 'sample_sigmas' parameter) and pass them when
#       present: sigma_v and the (shift_v, shift_a) tuple already carried on
#       _OutputState (model_aware.py), plus transformer_options['sample_sigmas']
#       (always set by comfy/samplers.py inner_sample). Backward compatible: on
#       pre-PDD ComfyUI cores (4-arg forward) the original 4-arg call is kept.
#
# Apply: cd <Spectrum checkout> && git apply /path/to/comfyui-spectrum-minimax-h3-pdd.patch
#       (or: patch -p1 < /path/to/comfyui-spectrum-minimax-h3-pdd.patch)
#
# Verification: applied to a fresh v0.2.20 copy - python -m py_compile passes;
#       detection helper verified against 4-arg and 7-arg stubs (True/False,
#       sample_sigmas at position 5, shifts at position 6); repo test suite
#       (tests/) run under the ComfyUI venv - see issue/commit notes for results.
#
diff --git a/comfyui_spectrum_h3/minimax_h3.py b/comfyui_spectrum_h3/minimax_h3.py
index ccb55bb..cdd5127 100644
--- a/comfyui_spectrum_h3/minimax_h3.py
